  "solution": {
    "text": "Two forms of D-glucopyranose are <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">α-</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D-</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>+-</mo></mrow></mfenced></math>glucopyranose and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">β-</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D-</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>+-</mo></mrow></mfenced></math>glucopyranose. These are anomers (a pair of stereoisomers which differ in configuration only around first-carbon atom are called anomers).<br /><br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/ci/image17-d43ee635-a482-4a48-8171-87187b4ef399.jpg\" style=\"width: 381px; height: 274px;\" />",
